 details:[['Correct gradient weighting','With equally sized local batches, averaging rank gradients matches the global mean. If valid token counts differ, use g = Σᵣ Bᵣgᵣ / ΣᵣBᵣ; a mean of local means can overweight short batches. DDP’s gradient averaging is separate from how your loss is normalized.'],['What is actually replicated','Ordinary DDP replicates parameters, gradients, and optimizer state. A distributed sampler prevents ranks from processing the same intended samples. Buffer broadcasts, such as BatchNorm-related state, are separate from gradient synchronization.']],
